    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n17770" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">fastōsus</span></b> , a, um, adj.
		2. fastus, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>full of</i>
			
			<i>pride</i>, <i>proud</i>, <i>haughty</i> (post-Aug. and rare): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">moecha,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Mart. 10, 13, 7</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">quid est, fastose?</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Petr. 131</span></i>
			.—<b>Transf.</b>, of things: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">domus, Auct. Pan. ad Pis. 107: garum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Mart. 13, 102, 2</span></i>
			.</div>
